---
- Remove KVM_PRE_FAULT_MEMORY call to keep up with API changes

- Reinette: Move tdx_read_capabilities() from "KVM: selftests: TDX: Use
  KVM_TDX_CAPABILITIES to validate TDs' attribute configuration" into this
  patch since TD creation depends on it. Move Isaku's "Suggested-by" tag
  with it but drop Binbin's "Reviewed-by" tag since the patch changed
  significantly. All other signatures are the same with Ackerley Tng
  already recognized as co-developer of this patch.

- Reinette: Squash Isakus' contribution to follow qemu tdx_mask_cpuid() and
  tdx_adjust_cpuid() @ qemu/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c to initialize cpuid
  array.  Export __tdx_mask_cpuid_features() for test cases that
  compares cpuid result. Add Co-developed-by to give attribution.

- Reinette: Squash Isaku's change to mimic QEMU to filter cpuid array.
  Otherwise KVM_TDX_INIT_VM fails. Drop kvm_tdx_init_vm_cpuid_data cpuid
  entry that the TDX module doesn't set directly. This is a catch-up
  for the KVM_TDX_INIT_VM change. Without this change KVM_TDX_INIT_VM
  results in EINVAL.

- Reinette: Squash Rick's fixup of CPUID struct to match KVM.
  Add Co-developed-by to give attribution.

- Reinette: Squash Isaku's change to export arch.s_bit to guest code.
  The guest needs shared bit.  Although the guest can use
  TDG.VP.VEINFO.GET(), it bloats guest code.  It simplifies the guest code
  to export the bits.

- Reinette: Squash Rick's change to remove KVM_CAP_MAX_VCPUS enable,
  it is no longer required/supported.

- Reinette: Add snippet to changelog to describe the changes made to
  CPUID entries.
