Date: Tue, 25 Jun 2024 01:59:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 100/115] KVM: selftests: TDX: Add shared memory test

Adds a test that sets up shared memory between the host and guest.

Co-developed-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
Change-Id: I95b15afb84790c046d4af2a58b03e57b5ea6439b
---
- Yan: rebased to tdx_kvm_dev-2024-06-21

- Reinette: Rebase on top of fixup to "KVM: selftests: TDX: Add
  report_fatal_error test" that removed handle_userspace_tdg_vp_vmcall_exit()
  due to handling of TDG_VP_VMCALL_REPORT_FATAL_ERROR no longer needed.
  Bring handle_userspace_tdg_vp_vmcall_exit() back to match original
  behavior to support original handling of TDG_VP_VMCALL_MAP_GPA.

- Reinette: Squash fix from Binbin to request KVM_HC_MAP_GPA_RANGE to
  exit to userspace for handling via KVM_CAP_EXIT_HYPERCALL and obtain
  needed parameters from returned hypercall arguments to call
  handle_memory_conversion() directly.
  For reference, KVM patches:
     KVM: x86: Check hypercall's exit to userspac
     KVM: TDX: Handle TDG.VP.VMCALL<MapGPA>
  Add attribution.
